   * from the todo_list_todos table.
   *
   * This endpoint allows an authenticated user to list their own Todo items,
   * retrieving them with advanced filtering options. Users may filter Todos by
   * completion status (completed or uncompleted) and due date range. All
   * results are strictly scoped to the requesting user's ownership, enforcing
   * privacy and preventing cross-user access.
   *
   * The operation enforces pagination for performance, with a maximum per-page
   * limit as specified in business rules (up to 50 items per page by default).
   * Sorting by creation date, completion status, and due date is supported for
   * flexible list organization.
   *
   * Only authenticated users are permitted to call this operation;
   * unauthenticated or expired tokens receive 401 errors. Users never see or
   * interact with any other user's data. All fields (description, completion
   * status, due date, timestamps) are present, with summary DTOs optimized for
   * bulk transfer. This operation relies entirely on the todo_list_todos
   * schema, with user reference integrity and business logic enforced by
   * backend providers.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param body Filter, search, and pagination parameters for retrieving the
   *   user's Todo list.
